{
  "name": "Track weekly competitor follower growth in Google Sheets and Slack with Juicer",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Weekly competitor growth tracker\nFor social media managers and agencies who report on competitor growth and are tired of copying follower counts by hand.\n\n### How it works\n1. Every Monday the workflow reads your list of competitor accounts.\n2. The Juicer node looks up each account and returns followers and post counts.\n3. Only exact handle matches are kept, so look-alike accounts never reach your report.\n4. One row per account is added to Google Sheets.\n5. The workflow compares each account with its previous row and posts a growth ranking to Slack.\n\n### Setup\nAbout 10 minutes.\n\n1. Add your Juicer API key (Developer page in Juicer) to **Look up competitor profiles**.\n2. In **Competitor accounts**, list one row per competitor and platform. Check each account's own bio first.\n3. Create a sheet with the columns week, competitor, platform, handle, followers, posts and url.\n4. Put the sheet URL and a Slack channel in **Your settings**, then connect Google Sheets and Slack.\n5. Click **Execute workflow** to test. The ranking starts from the second week.\n\nCredits per account: Instagram and TikTok 3, most others 1.\n\n### Requirements\n- A Juicer account with an API key\n- Google Sheets and Slack accounts\n\n### Customization tips\n- Run it daily for launches.\n- Add post counts or engagement to the ranking.\n\nThis template uses the verified Juicer community node (n8n-nodes-juicer). On self-hosted n8n, install it first under Settings > Community nodes.",
        "height": 900,
        "width": 460,
        "color": 1
      },
      "id": "6e65c310-86b6-5b39-9e23-63b6c9477bcb",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -700,
        -240
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
